  function MARKET_TEXT(){ return '<p>The Council Forum uses two currencies.</p>'+
    '<p><b>'+SYM.sov+' Sovereigns</b> and <b>'+SYM.crown+' Crowns</b> are the greater and lesser denominations of legal tender (ten Crowns to the Sovereign). They are struck for talk: opening a thread or leaving a comment in the Discussion, replying to another, or marking a passage. They are spent at <b>The Promenade</b>, located via the \u2696 in the Forum\u2019s radial menu. It is open all hours, and stocks a few things in limited number each month.</p>'+
    '<p><b>'+SYM.talent+' Talents</b> and <b>'+SYM.lira+' Lira</b> (ten Lira to the Talent) are contraband, and should be kept hidden at all times. They are struck for reading: every page turned in the Compendium. They are spent only with <b>The Shadow Merchant</b>, who keeps no shop. He is said to appear between nine in the evening and half past six in the morning, to those who are reading or talking at that hour, and never twice in a night. When he appears you will be told; when you leave him he is gone until another night. He carries rare art, cut material, a pass to new works before the rest, and \u2014 should the Writ weigh heavy \u2014 will sell a glass of water.</p>'+
    '<p class="hint">Coin is counted by the Imperial Reserve, not by you: short notes, hasty doubles and re-read pages earn nothing, and there is a daily measure to both.</p>'; }
